Built by openprinthq-desktops (apps/xtoolstudio): Wine on linuxserver.io's Selkies base, restyled for OpenPrintHQ, to run
xTool's xTool Studio for Windows. The repository and the image hold no copy of xTool Studio. The image built contains
the works below, each under its own licence, which the repository and the image keep.

linuxserver.io docker-baseimage-selkies
  https://github.com/linuxserver/docker-baseimage-selkies
  Copyright (C) linuxserver.io. GNU General Public License, version 3 (LICENSE).
  The image's base, its start-up scripts, its window manager settings (defaults/labwc.xml) and its web server
  set-up (etc/s6-overlay/s6-rc.d/init-nginx/run) are linuxserver.io's; common/restyle.py changes the last two
  as described in it. The repository's own files are offered under the same licence, GPL-3.0 (LICENSE).

Selkies
  https://github.com/selkies-project/selkies
  The web desktop and its dashboard (usr/share/selkies), Mozilla Public License 2.0 as published with it.
  The OpenPrintHQ dashboard is a copy of Selkies' own with one stylesheet added; Selkies' files are not changed.


xTool Studio
  https://www.xtool.com/pages/software
  xTool's software for its lasers, under xTool's own terms. Not in the image or the repository: the desktop's
  first start downloads xTool's Windows installer from xTool (the address and hash in apps/xtoolstudio/app.env)
  and installs it into the desktop's own storage. Its own first-run windows (country, terms and privacy policy,
  improvement plan) open blank under Wine, so apps/xtoolstudio/root/usr/local/lib/ahi/xtool_consent.py asks the
  person the same questions, showing the terms from xTool's installed files, and records only the answers the
  person gives, in xTool's own settings, as xTool's windows would.

xTool Studio LinuxBox
  https://github.com/AkitaEngineering/xTool-Studio-LinuxBox
  Copyright (C) 2026 Akita Engineering. GNU General Public License, version 3. Its findings on running xTool
  Studio under Wine (the Chromium graphics flags in apps/xtoolstudio/app.env, unpacking the app from the
  installer, and that the first-run windows are where Wine stops) informed this app's set-up; no code of it is
  copied.

Wine
  https://www.winehq.org
  Copyright (C) the Wine project authors. GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later, as published
  with it (opt/wine-stable/share/doc in the image). Installed as WineHQ's Debian packages, at the version in
  apps/xtoolstudio/upstream.env; its source is WineHQ's for that version. It is not changed.

Firefox ESR
  Debian's firefox-esr package, Mozilla Public License 2.0, used as the desktop's web browser.

Fonts
  Manrope, Sora and JetBrains Mono, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (the licence files are in the image next to the
  fonts, usr/share/selkies/artisanhub-dashboard/ahi/fonts).
